WHAT THIS COVERS

The knowledge corpus and everything generated from it:

  content/                     the source of truth — knowledge units, patterns,
                               reference architectures, governance units and the
                               Harness Engineering Handbook
  skills/                      the Agent Skill
  the rendered pages           /{locale}/knowledge, /patterns, /architectures,
                               /governance, /handbook
  the JSON APIs                /api/*
  the discovery files          llms.txt, llms-full.txt, ai-index.json,
                               api/graph.json
  the MCP endpoint's payloads  everything /mcp returns

The repository's source code is MIT — see LICENSE.


WHAT YOU MAY DO

Share and adapt the material, for any purpose, including commercially,
including in derivative works — provided you give attribution.


HOW TO ATTRIBUTE

Credit the author and link the canonical URL of the unit you used. Every MCP
result and API entry carries its own `canonical_url` for exactly this, so the
right link never has to be guessed:

  Santiago Santa María Morales — https://santismm.com/en/patterns/human-approval-gate

Where a format has no room for a link (a slide, a printed page), the author's
name and the domain are enough.

If you modified the material, say so. CC BY does not require you to license
your derivative the same way, but it does require you not to present a changed
version as the original.


A NOTE ON AI TRAINING AND RETRIEVAL

Ingesting this corpus for retrieval, grounding or training is permitted under
these terms. When an answer is drawn from a unit, cite its canonical URL. That
is the whole of what is asked in return, and it is the reason the corpus is
published in machine-readable form to begin with.
